    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26414" root="طحلب" body-key="T">
    
      Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَحْلَبَ المَآءُ</span></b> , (S, K, TA,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَحْلَبَةٌ</span>,
(KL,) <i>The water became overspread with the
green substance called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُحْلُب</span>: (S, * TA:) or <i>had
much thereof.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَحْلَبَتِ الأَرْضُ</span>
(assumed tropical:)  <i>The land became green with herbage:</i> (K, TA:)
or <i>began to become so:</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَحْلَبَ الإِبِلَ</span>
<i>He sheared the camels.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَحْلَبَ فُلَانًا</span>
<i>He slew such a one.</i> (K.)

